/// Term 6: "Fractions and Time" (Weeks 21-24) continues Year 1
/// Mathematics's pathway with two genuinely new strands introduced for
/// the first time: Week 21 teaches halves as splitting a shape or group
/// into 2 EQUAL parts (explicitly reusing Term 3 Week 9's equal-sides
/// framing and correcting the common "any 2 pieces" misconception);
/// Week 22 does the same for quarters, and connects 2 quarters back to
/// 1 half; Week 23 teaches reading an analogue clock for o'clock and
/// half past only; Week 24 is the capstone, combining all three into
/// one real-world scenario. Only halves and quarters of evenly-divisible
/// numbers are used (no thirds, eighths, or unlike-denominator
/// comparisons), and only o'clock/half past clock reading is used (no
/// quarter-past/quarter-to), matching this pathway's age-appropriate-
/// methods discipline.
