/// Term 3: "Everyday Materials" (Weeks 9-12) continues Year 1 Science's
/// pathway with a materials/chemistry-adjacent strand -- Week 9
/// introduces common everyday materials (wood, plastic, metal, glass,
/// fabric, paper) and what familiar objects are made of; Week 10 teaches
/// simple material properties (hard/soft, rough/smooth, bendy/stiff,
/// waterproof/not waterproof); Week 11 ties material properties to
/// real-world reasoning -- why a particular material is chosen for a
/// particular job (glass for windows because it's see-through, waterproof
/// fabric for umbrellas, metal or hard plastic for spoons); Week 12
/// closes the term with a capstone combining material types, properties,
/// and job-fit reasoning in one project-style story, the same way Term
/// 1's Week 4 and Term 2's Week 8 capstones worked.
