/// Term 4: "Weather and Seasons" (Weeks 13-16) continues Year 1 Science's
/// pathway with a weather/geography-adjacent strand grounded in Myanmar's
/// actual climate (three seasons, not the temperate four) -- Week 13
/// introduces observable weather types (sunny, rainy, cloudy, windy,
/// stormy); Week 14 teaches Myanmar's three seasons -- the Hot Season
/// (နွေရာသီ), the Rainy Season (မိုးရာသီ), and the Cool Season
/// (ဆောင်းရာသီ, explicitly not snowy); Week 15 ties weather/season
/// knowledge to real-world preparation -- choosing the right clothing
/// and gear (umbrella, raincoat, sunhat, light clothing, a jacket);
/// Week 16 closes the term with a capstone combining weather
/// observation, seasons, and preparation in one story, the same way
/// Term 1's Week 4, Term 2's Week 8, and Term 3's Week 12 capstones
/// worked.
